  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid variational quantum‑classical neural network using rotation and CNOT layers with up to 12 qubits and depth 8, evaluated on MNIST, CIFAR‑10, S&P500, and QM9. It reports 98.7% MNIST accuracy using ~1,250 parameters compared with 97.8% accuracy and ~25,000 parameters for a classical network, and claims ~47% training‑time reduction using staged training. Experiments were run using Qiskit on IBM quantum hardware (27‑ and 127‑qubit devices) and simulators.",
